{"abstract":"BACKGROUND AND PURPOSE: Proton therapy for breast cancer is usually given in free breathing (FB). With the use of deep inspiration breath-hold (DIBH) technique, the location of the heart is displaced inferiorly, away from the internal mammary nodes and, thus, the dose to the heart can potentially be reduced. The aim of this study was to explore the potential benefit of proton therapy in DIBH compared to FB for highly selected patients to reduce exposure of the heart and other organs at risk. We aimed at creating proton plans with delivery times feasible with treatment in DIBH. MATERIAL AND METHODS: Sixteen patients with left-sided breast cancer receiving loco-regional proton therapy were included. The FB and DIBH plans were created for each patient using spot-scanning proton therapy with 2-3 fields, robust and single field optimization. For the DIBH plans, minimum monitor unit per spot and spot spacing were increased to reduce treatment delivery time. RESULTS: All plans complied with target coverage constraints. The median mean heart dose was statistically significant reduced from 1.1 to 0.6 Gy relative biological effectiveness (RBE) by applying DIBH. No statistical significant difference was seen for mean dose and V17Gy RBE to the ipsilateral lung. The median treatment delivery time for the DIBH plans was reduced by 27% compared to the FB plans without compromising the plan quality. INTERPRETATION: The median absolute reduction in dose to the heart was limited. Proton treatment in DIBH may only be relevant for a subset of these patients with the largest reduction in heart exposure.","author_count":13,"contributors":["Stick, Line Bjerregaard","Nielsen, Louise Lærke","Trinh, Cecilia Bui","Bahij, Ihsan","Jensen, Maria Fuglsang","Kronborg, Camilla Jensenius Skovhus","Petersen, Stine Elleberg","Thai, Linh My Hoang","Martinsen, May Lin","Precht, Helle","Offersen, Birgitte Vrou"],"cuid":["S03-092.58-742005"],"filters":{"added":"2024-05","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":3,"corresponding_author":["Stick, Line Bjerregaard"],"keyword":["Breast cancer","Deep inspiration breath hold","Heart dose","Proton therapy"],"level":"sci","mra":["hum","med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U","DI-UC"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CDR"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-SDU"],"UC":["DI-UC-ALL","DI-UC-UCL"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CDR","DI-U-AU","DI-U-SDU","DI-UC-UCL"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"spot scanning proton therapy for early breast cancer in free breathing versus deep inspiration breath hold","src":["au","sdu","ucl"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-SDU","DI-UC-UCL"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.2340/1651-226X.2024.28591","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S03-092.58-742005","identifier":[{"id":"38404218","type":"pmid"},{"id":"PMC11332550","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"85186265220","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-b1f7f5f0-1323-468f-a94d-1afe5cd9d3dc","sdu-fcab04da-a3a8-4a1b-bee5-ea2a037a658f","ucl-0153a6e2-09b2-494f-8c1b-152b6899bb28"],"keyword":["Breast cancer","comparative treatment planning","deep inspiration breath-hold","heart dose","proton therapy"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Humanities","Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-6-48B5094CB4222D68111C2A263EB2E0BE"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.2340/1651-226X.2024.28591","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/256874149/document_3_.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"central denmark region","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CDR","l3nl":"Central Denmark Region","l3nn":"Central Denmark Region","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Central Denmark Region","namevar":["Aarhus University Hospital"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CDR","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"ucl university college","l2":"DI-UC","l2n":"University Colleges","l3":"DI-UC-UCL","l3nl":"UCL University College","l3nn":"UCL University College","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"UCL University College","namevar":["UCL University College"],"nora_code":"DI-UC-UCL","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Health, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine - DCPT - Danish Center for Particle Therapy"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"4","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Regional Health Research","SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Regional Health Research, IRS - Lillebælt Hospital, Research Unit of Radiology (Kolding)"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Line Bjerregaard","key":"stickpau","last":"Stick","name":"Stick, Line Bjerregaard","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Louise Lærke","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","name":"Nielsen, Louise Lærke","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Cecilia Bui","key":"trinhpau","last":"Trinh","name":"Trinh, Cecilia Bui","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3 1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Ihsan","key":"bahijpau","last":"Bahij","locid":"4473b82b-54a8-4e9b-ad00-be420ce0cb57","name":"Bahij, Ihsan","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3 1","corresponding":null,"first":"Maria Fuglsang","key":"jensenpau","last":"Jensen","locid":"84fbd618-5b11-42e5-99b0-40a94029c31d","name":"Jensen, Maria Fuglsang","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Maria","key":"fuglsangjensenpau","last":"Fuglsang Jensen","name":"Fuglsang Jensen, Maria","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3 1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Camilla Jensenius Skovhus","key":"kronborgpau","last":"Kronborg","locid":"9a9a4aa2-9e29-4c11-9210-34be3def937a","name":"Kronborg, Camilla","name_org":"Kronborg, Camilla Jensenius Skovhus","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3 1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Stine Elleberg","key":"petersenpau","last":"Petersen","locid":"c73d5422-4ca3-44de-884b-4fd97f024d05","name":"Petersen, Stine Elleberg","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Linh My Hoang","key":"thaipau","last":"Thai","name":"Thai, Linh My Hoang","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"May Lin","key":"martinsenpau","last":"Martinsen","locid":"6de0c4ce-9d93-4867-b733-12d8eecda1b3","name":"Martinsen, May-Lin","name_org":"Martinsen, May Lin","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 4","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Helle","key":"prechtpau","last":"Precht","locid":"c3c9d9f7-5dda-4eea-ad39-8278fd82c7cb","name":"Precht, Helle","orcid":"0000-0003-1525-5316","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3 1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Birgitte Vrou","key":"offersenpau","last":"Offersen","locid":"8e07074b-b750-43e0-93ec-b63086536def","name":"Offersen, Birgitte Vrou","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Birgitte Vrou","key":"offersendpau","last":"Offersend","name":"Offersend, Birgitte Vrou","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["38404218"],"pub":{"doi":"10.2340/1651-226x.2024.28591","issn":["0284186X","11001704"],"issn_org":["0284186X"],"journal":"Acta Oncologica","pages":"56-61","publisher":"Medical Journals Sweden AB","status":"p","title":"Acta Oncologica","title_org":"Acta oncologica (Stockholm, Sweden)","volume":"63"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85186265220"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","All University Colleges","Central Denmark Region","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","DI-UC","DI-UC-ALL","Hospitals","Region of Southern Denmark","UCL University College","Universities","University Colleges","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-b1f7f5f0-1323-468f-a94d-1afe5cd9d3dc","sdu-fcab04da-a3a8-4a1b-bee5-ea2a037a658f","ucl-0153a6e2-09b2-494f-8c1b-152b6899bb28"],"src":["AU Aarhus University","SDU University of Southern Denmark","UCL University College"],"title":"Spot-scanning proton therapy for early breast cancer in free breathing versus deep inspiration breath-hold","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S03-092.58-742005","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"INTRODUCTION: Childhood-onset obesity poses significant health risks, including early-onset type 2 diabetes, cardiovascular disease, and reduced quality of life. Hospital-based non-pharmacological obesity care can reduce childhood obesity, but 25% of children do not respond. Therefore, this study investigates the effect of the glucagon-like peptide-1 receptor agonist, semaglutide, as an add-on to hospital-based obesity care in youth who still have obesity following hospital-based obesity care as children. Furthermore, biomedical and psychosocial factors linked to treatment response will be investigated, alongside an exercise-based strategy to prevent weight regain and maintain a healthy body composition after semaglutide treatment. METHODS AND ANALYSIS: This is an investigator-initiated, randomised, placebo-controlled, double-blind trial. We will enrol expectedly 180-270 young adults aged 18-28 years based on their previous response to a paediatric obesity management programme and their current body mass index (BMI). Participants are categorised into four groups: low treatment response (BMI SD score (SDS) reduction <0.10; BMI ≥30 kg/m2); medium treatment response (BMI SDS reduction >0.25; BMI ≥30 kg/m2); high treatment response (BMI SDS reduction >0.50; BMI <30 kg/m2) and a population-based reference group with normal weight development in childhood. Participants with BMI ≥30 kg/m2 are randomised 2:1 to subcutaneous injections of semaglutide 2.4 mg/week or placebo as an add-on to hospital-based obesity care for 68 weeks. The primary outcome is the change in BMI from randomisation to the end of treatment with semaglutide compared with placebo. Secondary endpoints are changes in weight and body composition. ETHICS AND DISSEMINATION: The trial has been approved by the Danish Medicines Agency and the Ethical Committee of the Capital Region of Denmark (H-20039422). The trial will be conducted in accordance with the Declaration of Helsinki and follow the guidelines for Good Clinical Practice. Results will be presented at international scientific conferences and published in peer-reviewed scientific journals. TRIAL REGISTRATION NUMBER: EudraCT 2019-002274-31.","author_count":10,"contributors":["Byberg, Sarah","Holt, Joachim","Sandsdal, Rasmus Michael","Holm, Louise Aas","Madsen, Lærke Bruun","Christensen, Bodil Just","Jensen, Simon Birk Kjær","Hansen, Torben","Holm, Jens-Christian","Torekov, Signe Sørensen"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-779634"],"filters":{"added":"2025-01","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Body Mass Index","Obesity","Randomized Controlled Trial"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-OTH"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-OTH","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"protocol for a randomised double blinded controlled trial of youth with childhood onset obesity treated with semaglutide 000000000002 000000000004 mg week the resettle trial","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1136/bmjopen-2023-082446","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-779634","identifier":[{"id":"39551589","type":"pmid"},{"id":"PMC11574404","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"85209955425","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-ff1f9865-6da0-473d-869b-e37bd2c90cdb"],"keyword":["Body Mass Index","Obesity","Randomized Controlled Trial"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-DA2CCBA1B9A160758D3FA223A98A6B73"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/413555403/Protocol_for_a_randomised.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1136/bmjopen-2023-082446","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Biomedical Sciences, Torekov Group"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"other hospitals","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-OTH","l3nl":"Other Hospitals","l3nn":"Other Hospitals","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Other Hospitals","namevar":["Copenhagen University Hospital - Holbæk"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-OTH","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Sarah","key":"bybergsarahpau","last":"Byberg","locid":"f06174c4-506c-46c7-8805-97a0900e20da","name":"Byberg, Sarah","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Joachim","key":"holtjoachimpau","last":"Holt","locid":"ae8bb934-cd85-4557-a342-dd5ca6922444","name":"Holt, Joachim","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Rasmus Michael","key":"sandsdalrasmusmichaelpau","last":"Sandsdal","locid":"e1a6c85c-8801-466b-971b-65a2303b0527","name":"Sandsdal, Rasmus Michael","orcid":"0000-0003-0590-6285","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","first":"Louise Aas","key":"holmlouiseaaspau","last":"Holm","locid":"3c8db4dd-1b63-4f0c-8b8b-606ecb645ef9","name":"Holm, Louise Aas","orcid":"0000-0002-5439-5429","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Lærke Bruun","key":"madsenlærkebruunpau","last":"Madsen","locid":"bee51c87-f784-4e8a-a154-a8fcda8229c4","name":"Madsen, Lærke Bruun","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Bodil Just","key":"christensenbodiljustpau","last":"Christensen","locid":"610aa898-48ea-4ebe-86ff-4664cf197551","name":"Christensen, Bodil Just","orcid":"0000-0003-4529-8253","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Simon Birk Kjær","key":"jensensimonbirkkjærpau","last":"Jensen","locid":"9edd5734-2279-4744-b174-f70c08e9ad82","name":"Jensen, Simon Birk Kjær","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Torben","key":"hansentorbenpau","last":"Hansen","locid":"6b6bfff1-8b14-468b-af77-e71b375018e0","name":"Hansen, Torben","orcid":"0000-0001-8748-3831","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 1","first":"Jens Christian","key":"holmjenschristianpau","last":"Holm","locid":"d61af840-e87e-4a2e-8be2-b481959ef6c9","name":"Holm, Jens-Christian","name_org":"Holm, Jens Christian","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Signe","key":"torekovsignesørensenpau","last":"Torekov","locid":"c1d71a61-ee09-4c29-ae48-7520707a73be","name":"Torekov, Signe Sørensen","name_org":"Torekov, Signe","orcid":"0000-0001-6779-0252","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["39551589"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1136/bmjopen-2023-082446","issn":["20446055"],"issue":"11","journal":"BMJ Open","paperid":"e082446","status":"p","title":"BMJ Open","volume":"14"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85209955425"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Other Hospitals","Universities","University of Copenhagen","copenhagen university hospital - holbæk"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-ff1f9865-6da0-473d-869b-e37bd2c90cdb"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Protocol for a randomised, double-blinded, controlled trial of youth with childhood-onset obesity treated with semaglutide 2.4 mg/week : the RESETTLE trial","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-779634","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"Adult patients with Klinefelter syndrome (KS) are characterized by a highly variable phenotype, including tall stature, obesity, and hypergonadotropic hypogonadism, as well as an increased risk of developing insulin resistance, metabolic syndrome, and osteoporosis. Most adults need testosterone replacement therapy (TRT), whereas the use of TRT during puberty has been debated. In this retrospective, observational study, reproductive hormones and whole-body dual-energy x-ray absorptiometry-derived body composition and bone mineral content were standardized to age-related standard deviation scores in 62 patients with KS aged 5.9–20.6 years. Serum concentrations of total testosterone and inhibin B were low, whereas luteinizing hormone and follicle-stimulating hormone were high in patients before TRT. Despite normal body mass index, body fat percentage and the ratio between android fat percentage and gynoid fat percentage were significantly higher in the entire group irrespective of treatment status. In patients evaluated before and during TRT, a tendency toward a more beneficial body composition with a significant reduction in the ratio between android fat percentage and gynoid fat percentage during TRT was found. Bone mineral content (BMC) did not differ from the reference, but BMC corrected for bone area was significantly lower when compared to the reference. This study confirms that patients with KS have an unfavorable body composition and an impaired bone mineral status already during childhood and adolescence. Systematic studies are needed to evaluate whether TRT during puberty will improve these parameters.","author_count":13,"contributors":["Krabbe, Hans Valdemar López","Petersen, Jørgen Holm","Asserhøj, Louise Laub","Johannsen, Trine Holm","Christiansen, Peter","Jensen, Rikke Beck","Cleemann, Line Hartvig","Hagen, Casper P.","Priskorn, Lærke","Jørgensen, Niels","Main, Katharina M.","Juul, Anders","Aksglaede, Lise"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-689990"],"filters":{"added":"2023-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Body composition","Bone mineral content","Klinefelter syndrome"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"reproductive hormones bone mineral content body composition and testosterone therapy in boys and adolescents with klinefelter syndrome","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1530/EC-23-0031","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-689990","identifier":[{"id":"37010084","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85162766824","type":"scopus"},{"id":"PMC10305500","type":"pmcid"}],"ids":["ku-87dcf27d-869c-43ca-a787-e690d934e5e8"],"keyword":["Klinefelter syndrome","body composition","bone mineral content","truncal obesity"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-9E25CD5BA190921DCB360ABE8734B502"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1530/EC-23-0031","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/362680803/ec_EC_23_0031.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Copenhagen University Hospital - Rigshospitalet"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Public Health, Section of Biostatistics"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Hans Valdemar López","key":"krabbepau","last":"Krabbe","name":"Krabbe, Hans Valdemar López","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","first":"Jørgen Holm","key":"petersenpau","last":"Petersen","locid":"33c1c5b2-2e1e-4259-b4d7-04657a2bdb9b","name":"Petersen, Jørgen Holm","orcid":"0000-0003-3979-7443","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","first":"Louise Laub","key":"asserhøjpau","last":"Asserhøj","locid":"e82a767d-1fd5-4171-899a-dc443e28cc48","name":"Asserhøj, Louise Laub","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Trine Holm","key":"johannsenpau","last":"Johannsen","name":"Johannsen, Trine Holm","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Peter","key":"christiansenpau","last":"Christiansen","name":"Christiansen, Peter","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Rikke Beck","key":"jensenpau","last":"Jensen","name":"Jensen, Rikke Beck","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Line Hartvig","key":"cleemannpau","last":"Cleemann","name":"Cleemann, Line Hartvig","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Casper P.","key":"hagenpau","last":"Hagen","name":"Hagen, Casper P.","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Lærke","key":"priskornpau","last":"Priskorn","name":"Priskorn, Lærke","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Niels","key":"jørgensenpau","last":"Jørgensen","name":"Jørgensen, Niels","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","first":"Katharina M.","key":"mainpau","last":"Main","locid":"1770eebd-1659-4088-b44c-c9de22a4bb0b","name":"Main, Katharina M.","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","first":"Anders","key":"juulpau","last":"Juul","locid":"f9b11983-c7c8-4111-b119-4de471572898","name":"Juul, Anders","orcid":"0000-0002-0534-4350","rank":12,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Lise","key":"aksglaedepau","last":"Aksglaede","name":"Aksglaede, Lise","rank":13,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["37010084"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1530/ec-23-0031","issn":["20493614"],"issue":"7","journal":"Endocrine Connections","paperid":"e230031","status":"p","title":"Endocrine Connections","volume":"12"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85162766824"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-87dcf27d-869c-43ca-a787-e690d934e5e8"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Reproductive hormones, bone mineral content, body composition, and testosterone therapy in boys and adolescents with Klinefelter syndrome","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-689990","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"BACKGROUND: Patient-reported Outcome (PRO) measures may be used as the basis for out-patient follow-up instead of fixed appointments. The patients attend follow-up from home by filling in questionnaires developed for that specific aim and patient group (telePRO). The questionnaires are handled in real time by a specific algorithm, which assigns an outcome color reflecting clinical need. The specific questionnaires and algorithms (named solutions) are constructed in a consensus process with clinicians. We aimed to describe AmbuFlex' telePRO solutions and the algorithm outcomes and variation between patient groups, and to discuss possible applications and challenges. METHODS: TelePRO solutions with more than 100 processed questionnaires were included in the analysis. Data were retrieved together with data from national registers. Characteristics of patients, questionnaires and outcomes were tabulated for each solution. Graphs were constructed depicting the overall and within-patient distribution of algorithm outcomes for each solution. RESULTS: From 2011 to 2021, 29 specific telePRO solutions were implemented within 24 different ICD-10 groups. A total of 42,015 patients were referred and answered 171,268 questionnaires. An existing applicable instrument with cut-off values was available for four solutions, whereas items were selected or developed ad hoc for the other solutions. Mean age ranged from 10.7 (Pain in children) to 73.3 years (chronic kidney disease). Mortality among referred patients varied between 0 (obesity, asthma, endometriosis and pain in children) and 528 per 1000 patient years (Lung cancer). There was substantial variation in algorithm outcome across patient groups while different solutions within the same patient group varied little. DISCUSSION: TelePRO can be applied in diseases where PRO can reflect clinical status and needs. Questionnaires and algorithms should be adapted for the specific patient groups and clinical aims. When PRO is used as replacement for clinical contact, special carefulness should be observed with respect to patient safety.","author_count":20,"contributors":["Hjollund, Niels Henrik I.","Larsen, Louise Pape","de Thurah, Annette Ladefoged","Grove, Birgith Engelst","Skuladottir, Halla","Linnet, Hanne","Friis, Rasmus Blechingberg","Johnsen, Søren Paaske","May, Ole","Jensen, Annesofie Lunde","Hansen, Troels Krarup","Taarnhøj, Gry Assam","Tolstrup, Lærke Kjær","Pappot, Helle","Ivarsen, Per","Dørflinger, Liv","Jessen, Anne","Sørensen, Nanna Toxvig","Schougaard, Liv Marit Valen","Team, The AmbuFlex"],"cuid":["S03-099.42-685568"],"filters":{"added":"2023-02","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":3,"corpau":["The AmbuFlex team"],"corresponding_author":["Hjollund, Niels Henrik I."],"keyword":["Algorithm","Chronic Disease","Decision support systems","Malignant diseases","Outpatient follow up","Patient Reported Outcome Measures","Questionnaires"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-NP","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-CDR","DI-HO-STENO"],"NP":["DI-NP-ALL","DI-NP-CAN"],"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-CDR","DI-HO-STENO","DI-NP-CAN","DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"patient reported outcome pro measurements in chronic and malignant diseases ten years experience with pro algorithm based patient clinician interaction telepro in ambuflex","src":["aau","au","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1007/s11136-022-03322-9","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S03-099.42-685568","identifier":[{"id":"85146283230","type":"scopus"},{"id":"PMC10063508","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"36639598","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["aau-07951fa2-17fb-48b1-8f18-