enmark"],"title":"Virkemidler til reduktion af fosforbelastningen af vandmiljøet","type":"Report","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-092.00-767259","year":"2020","yearsub":"2020"}
{"abstract":"Parkinson's disease, dementia with Lewy bodies, and multiple system atrophy comprise a group of neurodegenerative diseases termed synucleinopathies. Synucleinopathie are, characterized by presence of inclusion bodies in degenerating brain cells which contain aggregated α-synuclein phosphorylated on Ser129. Although the inflammation-associated serine-threonine kinase, PKR (EIF2AK2), promotes cellular protection against infection, we demonstrate a pro-degenerative role of activated PKR in an α-synuclein-dependent cell model of multiple system atrophy, where inhibition and silencing of PKR decrease cellular degeneration. In vitro phosphorylation demonstrates that PKR can directly bind and phosphorylate monomeric and filamenteous α-synuclein on Ser129. Inhibition and knockdown of PKR reduce Ser129 phosphorylation in different models (SH-SY5Y ASYN cells, OLN-AS7 cells, primary mouse hippocampal neurons, and acute brain slices), while overexpression of constitutively active PKR increases Ser129 α-syn phosphorylation. Treatment with pre-formed α-synuclein fibrils, proteostatic stress-promoting MG-132 and known PKR activators, herpes simplex virus-1-∆ICP34.5 and LPS, as well as PKR inducer, IFN-β-1b, lead to increased levels of phosphorylated Ser129 α-synuclein that is completely blocked by simultaneous PKR inhibition. These results reveal a direct link between PKR and the phosphorylation and toxicity of α-synuclein, and they support that neuroinflammatory processes play a role in modulating the pathogenicity of α-synuclein.","author_count":11,"contributors":["Reimer, Lasse","Vesterager, Louise Buur","Betzer, Cristine","Zheng, Jin","Nielsen, Lærke Dalsgaard","Kofoed, Rikke Hahn","Lassen, Louise Berkhoudt","Bølcho, Ulrik","Paludan, Søren R","Fog, Karina","Jensen, Poul Henning"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-145690"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Alpha synuclein","Cytotoxicity","Neurodegeneration","PKR","Phosphorylation","Synucleinopathies"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"OT":["Unspecified organisation"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"inflammation kinase pkr phosphorylates α synuclein and causes α synuclein dependent cell death","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85044018602","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-145690","identifier":[{"id":"85044018602","type":"scopus"},{"id":"29501855","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["au-1c96923e-054b-4583-a83c-1e01a9d59a7a"],"keyword":["Alpha-Synuclein","Cytotoxicity","EIF2AK2","Neurodegeneration","PKR","Phosphorylation","Synucleinopathies"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-CD880F08E8D826F23747D3F5D2A3E719"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2018","yearSub":"2018"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Health, Department of Biomedicine","Aarhus University, Interfaculty Centre, DANDRITE, DANDRITE - Jensen Group"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"miscellaneous","l2":"DI-OT","l2n":"Miscellaneous","l3":"DI-OT","l3nl":"Other Research","l3nn":"Miscellaneous","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Miscellaneous","namevar":["Unspecified organisation"],"nora_code":"DI-OT","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Lasse","key":"reimerpau","last":"Reimer","locid":"cedd886b-70e4-4ea0-b9e4-8457c064b8f6","name":"Reimer, Lasse","orcid":"0000-0002-6996-3185","rank":1,"rolecode"